// The collections conformance package. Its `test/` directory calls every
// exported name of the collection modules — which the `stdlib` suite cannot,
// because it stops after type checking and a body-less declaration with no
// runtime function behind it passes that silently.
//
// **There is no comparison counter here, and there cannot be one.** A count
// needs somewhere to live, Buri has no mutation, and a lambda may not capture a
// context (SPEC 10.6) — so the only counter-outside-the-value in the language
// is `core/alloc`'s handle. Hanging one on a key and charging it from
// `Ordered.compare` does compile, and it does not work: `compare` and `hash` take
// no context, so they are pure by signature and the compiler is free to drop a
// redundant call, which it does — differently in different shapes of the same
// program. A test built on that would report a number that moved when the
// optimizer moved. So the cost claims are pinned by what a *value* can show:
// the answer, the order, and agreement with the naive computation over inputs
// large enough to have gone down every path.
